## 1. Longform — fix the break (highest priority; it's been down a while)

- [x] **Run the diagnostic to find the cause.** *(Done 2026-07-04.)* Two causes, both confirmed live against the API:
  - **(d) dead key** — the OpenRouter key returns HTTP 401 "User not found" (revoked or account deleted). The Nightly Judgement kept working anyway because `run-judgements.js` falls back to the `claude` CLI when no key is set — longform had no such fallback, so it was the only casualty.
  - **(b) bad model slug** — `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6` doesn't exist on OpenRouter; the real slug is `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6` (dot, not hyphen). Would have 404'd even with a live key.
- [x] **Apply the fix.** *(Done 2026-07-04.)* `run-longform.cjs` now falls back to the `claude` CLI when `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is unset (same pattern as `run-judgements.js`), the slug is corrected for when a working key is supplied, `max_tokens` raised 3000→6000 (3000 could truncate a 2,200-word essay), portraits resolve from `voices.html` first (works offline/sandboxed), and a missing `dotenv` install no longer crashes the script. Clean end-to-end run confirmed: Hume episode written + index card inserted.
  - **Still on you:** to restore OpenRouter mode for local Windows runs, generate a fresh key at openrouter.ai and put it in `.env` — the old `sk-or-v1-2950…` key is dead. The CLI fallback needs no key.
- [x] **Fold the diagnostic error-handling into the real `run-longform.cjs`.** *(Done 2026-07-04.)* Failures now report HTTP status + OpenRouter error body instead of being swallowed.

## 2. Longform — quality upgrade (after it connects again)

- [ ] **Make longform load the real persona `.md` system prompts.** Currently `fetchEpisode()` reconstructs a thin prompt from the persona *name only* (`You are ${name}...`) and never reads the authored `.md`. Result: longform ignores all the persona work and leans on the model's generic knowledge. Change: read the persona's identity prompt, prepend it to the essay-format instructions.
  - Payoff: the modernised prompts then drive all three outputs, not just Judgement + chatbot.

## 3. Persona roster — reconcile the three-way mismatch

- [ ] **The three files disagree on who exists.** `run-judgements.js` knows 18 personas; `run-longform.cjs` knows 27; `run-longform.bat` help text lists 28. Membership conflicts too (e.g. `marx` is in longform but not judgements; judgements uses id `adamsmith`, longform uses `smith`).
  - Pick one canonical roster (likely `personas.json` or a shared module), have all runners read from it, so a persona can't silently exist in one mode and not another.

## 4. Persona prompts — deploy this session's work

Seven modernised prompts + one new build, produced 2026-06-26. All are format-free identity prompts (correct for the Salon's bolt-the-format-on-at-runtime architecture).

- [ ] **Deploy modernised prompts:** Wollstonecraft, Parker, James (longform-shaped), Hume, Voltaire.
- [ ] **Deploy Machiavelli — two files:** `machiavelli-advisor` (standalone Strategic Advisor, keeps its own 4-section/Fortuna's Share contract) and `machiavelli-salon` (Judgement-format variant). Make sure each lands in the right place; don't cross them.
- [ ] **Deploy Austen** — new build from research: `austen-persona.md` + `austen-factsheet.rtf`. FID filter is the central analytical move.
- [ ] **Note on Dante:** modernised with the archaic register *dropped* (deliberate). Dry-run a judgement or two before trusting it live — register change was the one load-bearing edit. Imagery vocab (mirror of vanity, abyss of echoes) kept; persona diction modernised.

