## 9. Mobile format odd on the right hand of the screen
- [x] *(Done 2026-07-05.)* Cause: `.site-nav` is a centred flex row of `white-space: nowrap` links — five links exceed a phone's width and centred overflow spills off *both* edges, widening the whole page. Fixed on all five pages (index, voices, salon-index, longform, longform/index) + the episode template in `run-longform.cjs`: below 640px the nav wraps, dividers hide, link padding tightens, and the masthead dateline gets clearance so the theme dots no longer overlap it. Verified headless at 412px: no horizontal overflow on any page.

